## Table of Contents
Stable and redox active metal–organic frameworks were constructed by incorporating $Z r_{6}$ clusters and redox-active TTF-based linkers, which allow in-situ generation and stabilization of ultra-small noble metal nanoparticles for heterogenous catalysis.
